---
layout: base.njk
title: "CDC Glossary — terms, aliases, and where they come up"
description: "Vendor-agnostic definitions for the CDC vocabulary: WAL, LSN, tombstones, snapshots, exactly-once vs. effectively-once, and the rest. Anchor links per term."
canonicalPath: "/glossary/"
---
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}

{{ ui.hero({
  title: "CDC Glossary",
  description: "<p>The vocabulary you need to talk about Change Data Capture without hand-waving. Definitions stay vendor-agnostic where they can and call out the specific name each database/broker uses where they can't.</p>",
  align: "center",
  skillLevel: "Reference"
}) | safe }}

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="glossary-intro">
  <h2 id="glossary-intro" class="visually-hidden">About this glossary</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Each entry has a stable anchor. Deep-link from a module page or a
    Slack thread with <code>/glossary/#tombstone</code> and the reader
    lands on the definition directly. Aliases list other names you'll
    see in the wild; "see also" cross-links the related entries.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="glossary-terms">
  <h2 id="glossary-terms" class="visually-hidden">Definitions</h2>
  <dl class="glossary">
    {% set sortedTerms = glossary | sort(false, true, "term") %}
    {% for entry in sortedTerms %}
      <dt id="{{ entry.slug }}" class="glossary__term">
        <a class="glossary__anchor" href="#{{ entry.slug }}" aria-label="Permalink to {{ entry.term }}">#</a>
        {{ entry.term }}
        {% if entry.aliases and entry.aliases.length %}
          <span class="glossary__aliases">
            (also: {% for alias in entry.aliases %}<code>{{ alias }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      </dt>
      <dd class="glossary__definition">
        {{ entry.definition | safe }}
        {% if entry.related and entry.related.length %}
          <p class="glossary__related">
            See also:
            {% for slug in entry.related %}
              {%- set ref = null -%}
              {%- for candidate in glossary -%}
                {%- if candidate.slug == slug -%}{% set ref = candidate %}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {% if ref %}<a href="#{{ ref.slug }}">{{ ref.term }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </dd>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="glossary-howto">
  <h2 id="glossary-howto">Missing a term?</h2>
  <p>
    The glossary is data-driven — add entries to
    <code>src/_data/glossary.mjs</code> and the page picks them up at
    build time. Anchor IDs are stable: don't rename a <code>slug</code>
    after it's been linked to externally.
  </p>
</section>
